WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:06.379
As a result of this player's history
DDoS activity, abusive behavior and poor

00:00:06.379 --> 00:00:10.400
sportsmanship, the player behavior team
has issued a lifetime ban on Jensen.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:14.720
His account has been perma banned and
all future accounts will be permabanned on site.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:19.460
Jensen has consistently disregarded the letter and spirit of the Summoner's Code.

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:22.820
His disrespect for the
rules of the game is unacceptable for

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:27.050
any player, especially a high profile
eSports competitor who has a regular

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:29.920
opportunity to lead the community by
example.

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:39.960
Nikolaj Jensen has become of the West's strongest Mid laners, and players for one of the league's most iconic teams.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:47.480
(Casting)

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:53.100
But unlike some of his contemporaries the journey he took to get there was anything but standard.

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:56.120
Jensen: But unfortunately we got disqualified as a

00:00:56.120 --> 00:01:02.500
team and a few members of the team,
including me got banned due to toxic behavior.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:06.760
The former World of WarCraft
arena enthusiast used the alias of Veigodx

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:11.570
in his early League of Legends days.
Jensen became known for his solo queue play

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:17.600
in Season 2, especially his 1v1 out plays.
And helped found a roster called Team

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:23.060
Solo Mebdi, which included players such as
Nukeduck, YamatoCannon, and Rayt3ch.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:26.840
The team was set to compete in the
qualifiers for the Season Three European

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:32.720
Championship Series. It was the first
split of the LCS in Europe and qualification was a big deal.

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:35.510
Joe Miller: To earn a
spot in the qualifying rounds the teams

00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:39.680
have had to battle their way through the
online qualifiers all placed highly in

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:42.300
those major tournaments throughout the
preseason.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:47.580
Though competition had existed for European teams before Season 3, it was never like this.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.780
This was a major opportunity.

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:53.720
Unfortunately for Jensen it
wasn't an opportunity he would get.

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:57.170
A competitive ruling from Riot Games
banned him from competitive play

00:01:57.170 --> 00:02:02.000
indefinitely, and Team Solo Mebdi was
disqualified from the competition.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:06.320
The Riot Games ruling said that Jensen had
consistently disregarded the letter and

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:10.459
spirit of the summoner's code. His
disrespect for the rules of the game is

00:02:10.459 --> 00:02:15.770
unacceptable for any player, especially a
high profile eSports competitor who has

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:20.269
a regular opportunity to lead the
community by example. Riot said that

00:02:20.269 --> 00:02:25.340
Jensen had publicly and unapologetically
admitted to engaging in a series of DDoS

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:30.769
attacks against high elo players. Jensen
admitted to having threatened DDoS in an

00:02:30.769 --> 00:02:34.000
interview with in2LOL shortly
afterwards.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.720
But said he never actually did it.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:44.920
Jensen: After that I felt really down. I definitely learned a lot about myself as a person.

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:47.520
Not only was his Veigodx account banned,

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:52.120
but all future accounts belonging to
Jensen would be banned on site as well.

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:57.530
It was a lifetime ban in all senses of
the term. This was a big departure from

00:02:57.530 --> 00:03:01.910
previous Riot bans where players like IWillDominate had been allowed a new

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:07.340
start under a different alias, which
Jensen was denied. Jensen's future as a

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:11.510
competitive player seemed done. Left
without any real options

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:15.760
Jensen found another way to leave his
mark on the competitive scene. Though the

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:20.870
exact date is unclear, Jensen became the
coach of SK gaming. A fact that was

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:24.590
discovered by fans of the competitive
scene, though it was not formally

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:29.090
announced at the time. The initial ruling
against Jensen had stated that he was

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:34.430
ineligible to compete in the LCS and in
any Riot affiliated League of Legends

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:39.020
tournaments indefinitely. This suspension
shall commence immediately.

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:44.440
Whether coaching qualified as competition was
unclear. In Korea however where worlds

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:49.310
was to be held that year, coaching was
already recognized and according to Riot

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:53.440
that meant that Jensen was banned from
being officially recognized as a coach

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:58.700
despite the fact that he had already
been part of SK staff if informally up

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:03.920
to that point. Their explanation he had
been granted access to the EU LCS studio

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:10.100
during Season Four as a team guest. Also,
team guests would not be allowed for Worlds.

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:14.460
But according to an AMA he did
in October 2014, he had previously

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:18.370
reached an agreement with Riot that
allowed him to play the game without the

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:23.050
ban on site provision. While he wasn't
allowed to compete, his new accounts

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:26.960
would no longer be targeted as long as he
maintained his behavior.

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:31.420
Riot Games banned policy underwent a big change in
late November 2014.

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:36.160
Instead of permanently banning players
from competitive play and issuing ban on

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:41.290
site orders, Riot instead changed those
bans to indefinite bans meaning that

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:46.320
they would be reviewable at a later date
if players' conduct on their new accounts was acceptable.

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:50.040
Jensen was finally
allowed to stream and his ban came up

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:54.370
for review under the new policy, but
according to riot he did not yet meet

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:59.470
the criteria to be unbanned. Still riot
said his case would be reviewable five

00:04:59.470 --> 00:05:03.920
weeks before the beginning of the LCS
Summer Split.

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:23.980
The team he would eventually join, Cloud 9 had a rollercoaster Spring Split in 2015.

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:28.640
Hai, the team's midlaner had long acted as the primary shot-caller.

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:32.020
C9 managed a
second-place finish in the Spring Playoffs.

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:42.940
(Casting)

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:47.419
But Hai then step down from the
active roster citing a wrist injury.

00:05:47.419 --> 00:05:52.370
The roster that had played together since
April 2013 had made its first major move

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:57.200
and Jensen was set to become the first
of a second generation of Cloud 9 players.

00:05:57.200 --> 00:06:02.560
Jensen: After I got unbanned I was lucky
enough to get picked up by Cloud 9.

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:14.680
I want the best for C9 and I'll do everything I can to help support them get to where we're supposed to be.

00:06:17.560 --> 00:07:11.640
(Casting)

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:17.880
Although statistically Jensen had an above-average season, it became clear that Hai had been more than

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:21.979
just the team's mid laner. He was a key
part of their shot calling and strategy

00:07:21.979 --> 00:07:24.979
the team sometimes seemed lost without
him.

00:07:24.979 --> 00:07:30.020
Relegation became a real possibility and
the team needed Hai back, but it wasn't

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:33.800
Jensen who would step aside,
it was the jungler Meteos.

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:38.280
Sneaky: I don't think, I don't know if Meteos, is like out.

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:43.680
But I think we're trying this.

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:46.140
The
change didn't instantly turn Cloud 9 around,

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:50.060
but putting Hai in at the jungler
position gave the team enough momentum

00:07:50.060 --> 00:07:52.400
to avoid the promotion tournaments.

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:53.880
Jensen: Meteos is still a great jungler.

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:59.360
They have a bit of a different style where Hai
is much more supportive I would say.

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:04.069
But the major thing was like the shotcalling, 
but also Hai used to be a mid laner so he

00:08:04.069 --> 00:08:07.460
understands what I need and he can
like help me much more and it's easier

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:09.660
for him to understand when you have to help me as well.

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:14.240
After winning a tiebreaker against Team 8 they placed seventh in the regular season

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:19.009
not playoff bound, but not facing down
relegation. However C9 had earned enough

00:08:19.009 --> 00:08:22.969
championship points to make it to the
North American Regional Gauntlet and

00:08:22.969 --> 00:08:25.720
there the team would finally find their
stride.

00:08:25.720 --> 00:09:18.760
(Casting)

00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:20.400
Jensen was a key part of the team's

00:09:20.420 --> 00:09:24.950
efforts as they reverse swept both
Gravity Gaming and Team Impulse before

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:27.400
winning three and one against Team
Liquid.

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:33.640
Jensen: Man I'm super happy right now, like I don't even realize it myself I think, but I don't know I'm just so happy right now.

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:36.760
Against all odds Cloud 9 had made it to worlds.

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:43.580
Jensen's first season with the team despite rocky team dynamics, showed flashes of brilliance.

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:45.600
Hai: And I'm actually pretty surprised at how

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:49.280
Jensen took the games, he was 0 - 2,
like aight dudes we're going in now, we're

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:55.080
gonna win. I was like I can appreciate
that so everyone had a very good mentaltiy for the 0 - 2.

00:09:55.080 --> 00:10:01.440
Think about that for a moment, in Jensen's past he had grappled with controlling his emotions.

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:04.040
By his own admission he had been a toxic player.

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:08.300
Jensen: But I think I have a
lot to improve on still so I think the

00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:12.040
main goal is to be good at good for Worlds for world so we'll see.

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:17.200
But during his rookie split one game away from elimination he chose a different path.

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:19.600
Jensen: We might start out a bit slow, but

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:25.020
I think by the end of the season we will
be one of the best if not the best team In NA

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:28.860
He chose to cheer on his teammates and it had worked.

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:33.400
Jensen had become the first permanently banned player to be redeemed.

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:35.480
Hai: I think in the
beginning of the season Jensen was a

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:39.950
little nervous to play had a lot of big
shoes to fill up basically and I don't

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:42.360
know how his team was there to help him
up that much.

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:48.500
At Worlds Cloud9 got off to a hot start in Group B with three straight wins. The next week they

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:54.900
followed that up with three losses and
then were eliminated in the tiebreaker by AHQ e-sports club.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:11:08.120
(Casting)

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:10.320
The Gauntlet
and Worlds may have been a Cinderella

00:11:10.339 --> 00:11:15.649
run for the team, but Spring 2016 broke
up much of the original Cloud 9 roster.

00:11:15.649 --> 00:11:21.079
Hai and Balls were moved to Cloud 9
Challenger. Meteos returned as jungler and

00:11:21.079 --> 00:11:26.540
Impact was added to the roster as the
new top laner. 2016 saw Jensen settle

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:31.339
into his role as C9 starting mid laner
and changed his alias from Incarnation.

00:11:31.339 --> 00:11:36.230
He earned all pro team honors in the
Spring Split and the team 5th - 6th in

00:11:36.230 --> 00:11:40.339
Spring Playoffs and second in Summer,
earning another trip to the Gauntlet and

00:11:40.339 --> 00:11:45.709
yet another trip to Worlds. He also set a
new record for kills in a single game

00:11:45.720 --> 00:12:03.480
(Casting)

00:12:03.480 --> 00:12:08.940
While Jensen's behavior had been reformed his
signature cockiness remains.

00:12:08.940 --> 00:12:13.360
Jensen: Yeah I would say I would say I'm pretty cocky when it comes to the game, yeah.

00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:18.720
Thorin: And what is that based on then, just knowing you're better? Thinking you're better?

00:12:18.720 --> 00:12:21.500
Jensen: Yeah I would say I would say it's a mix of both.

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:27.380
Going into Worlds 2016 Jensen expressed his intention to defeat Faker in lane on Twitter.

00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:31.180
A now notorious comment especially given the outcome.

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:33.100
Jensen: If you want to prove yourself you have

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:37.840
to beat Faker and that's like one
opportunity I get so that's what I'm going to do.

00:12:37.840 --> 00:13:15.040
(Casting)

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:18.140
The team ultimately went out in Quarterfinals that year,

00:13:18.140 --> 00:13:24.020
and while Jensen didn't clap Faker he has shown continued improvement over his time in the NA LCS.

00:13:24.020 --> 00:13:30.840
He was neck and neck with Bjergsen in the Spring Split, and statistically the best NA LCS Mid laner in Summer.

00:13:30.840 --> 00:13:34.560
Ultimately Jensen showed
us that redemption is possible.

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:39.540
Even for those who receive some of the harshest
punishments that Riot Games has ever issued.

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:43.740
Not only that, but his route to
that success showed us that he may even

00:13:43.740 --> 00:13:49.280
have become a better player and teammate
in the process.

00:13:51.120 --> 00:14:02.540
Thanks for watching if you want more
great content be sure to hit that subscribe button.

